---
import DocumentLayout from '../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL, APP_STORE_AVAILABLE, APP_ARCHIVER_URL, DEVELOPER_URL } from '../consts';
const sections = [
  { id: 'agreement', label: 'Agreement and app license' }, { id: 'product', label: 'What DiskPress does' },
  { id: 'responsibilities', label: 'Your responsibilities' }, { id: 'results', label: 'Results and limitations' },
  { id: 'purchases', label: 'Mac App Store version' }, { id: 'setapp', label: 'Setapp version' },
  { id: 'privacy', label: 'Privacy and other services' },
  { id: 'warranties', label: 'Warranties and liability' }, { id: 'updates', label: 'Updates and contact' },
];
---
<DocumentLayout title="Terms of service" eyebrow="Terms of service" heading="Clear expectations. In your control." description="Terms for DiskPress and its website, with separate licensing and payment information for the Mac App Store and Setapp versions. Keep an independent backup before optimizing files." sections={sections} updated="September 20, 2026">
  <section id="agreement"><h2>Agreement and application license</h2><p>These terms describe use of diskpress.app and the Mac App Store and Setapp versions of the DiskPress macOS application, provided by <a href={DEVELOPER_URL}>Ighor July</a>. By using the website or application, you agree to the applicable terms. If you do not agree, do not use them.</p><p>The product guidance and responsibilities below apply to both versions. Licensing, payments, and access depend on where you obtained the app. Read the <a href="#purchases">Mac App Store</a> or <a href="#setapp">Setapp</a> section for your version. These terms do not override the applicable distribution terms or any non-waivable legal rights.</p></section>
  <section id="product"><h2>What DiskPress does</h2><p>DiskPress optimizes supported local files through native lossless filesystem compression and clone-based deduplication. You select files, authorize locations, configure settings, and decide whether to run one-time work, command-line operations, or automatic monitoring.</p><p>Optimization changes a file's physical storage representation while preserving its logical contents and path. It may replace a file with a verified compressed or cloned version and remove the temporary original after successful completion. It is not a backup service, archive manager, file-recovery product, or general Undo system.</p><p>Application bundles, executables, system locations, and other protected or unsupported targets are excluded. <a href={APP_ARCHIVER_URL}>App Archiver</a> is a separate product for supported Mac applications and is subject to its own terms.</p></section>
  <section id="responsibilities"><h2>Your responsibilities</h2><ul><li>Only process files you own or have permission to modify. Respect other people's rights and any applicable software, data, or organizational restrictions.</li><li>Maintain an independent, usable backup of important data before optimization. Verification and recovery safeguards do not eliminate every storage risk.</li><li>Choose locations and exclusions carefully. Review initial results before enabling recurring or scripted work.</li><li>Allow cancellations and recovery operations to finish. Preserve any material identified by an unresolved recovery message.</li><li>Control any scripts or AI agents you authorize. Their commands can change file storage just as manual optimization can.</li></ul><p>Do not use the website or app to interfere with another person's data, evade access controls, infringe rights, or violate applicable law. These terms do not restrict activities that the law or an applicable open-source license expressly permits.</p></section>
  <section id="results"><h2>Results and compatibility</h2><p>There is no guaranteed compression ratio, amount of free space, processing speed, or compatibility with every file and volume. Files may be skipped or produce no useful saving. Example screenshots and possible percentage savings illustrate outcomes, not a commitment about your Mac.</p><p>Deduplication savings are estimates of shared storage. macOS available space, reclaimable space, current measured savings, and recent optimization history are different measurements. Snapshots, filesystem accounting, and concurrent writes may affect the result you see.</p><p>Existing compression and sharing can remain after DiskPress quits. Later edits, replacements, copies, updates, or third-party software may change or remove those savings. Current compatibility and behavior are described in the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> and the installed version's help.</p></section>
  <section id="purchases">
    <h2>Mac App Store version</h2>
    <h3>License and purchases</h3>
    <p>DiskPress downloaded from the Mac App Store is licensed under <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/">Apple's Standard End User License Agreement</a>, unless the App Store listing supplies a different applicable license. These website terms supplement, but do not replace, that license.</p>
    {!APP_STORE_AVAILABLE && <p>DiskPress will be available soon on the Mac App Store and is awaiting approval. It is not yet available to download or purchase there. The purchase and refund information below applies once it is released.</p>}
    <p>Apple processes Mac App Store purchases and applies its <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/">Media Services Terms</a>. {APP_STORE_AVAILABLE ? 'Check the listing for the current price and regional availability.' : 'The listing will show the price and regional availability once it is live.'} No Setapp subscription is required to use this version. The website does not collect payment-card information.</p>
    <h3>Refunds and billing help</h3>
    <p>For an App Store refund, use <a href="https://support.apple.com/118223">Apple's refund request process</a>. Eligibility follows Apple's policies and applicable law. Setapp does not manage Mac App Store purchases or refunds.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="setapp">
    <h2>Setapp version</h2>
    <h3>License and continued access</h3>
    <p>For this version, the developer grants you a non-exclusive license to install and use DiskPress on Macs you own or control, within the access rights provided by your valid Setapp entitlement and subject to these terms. Apple's App Store license does not apply to this version.</p>
    <p>Your Setapp account, permitted devices, subscription, and continued access are governed by <a href="https://setapp.com/terms-of-use">Setapp's terms of use</a> and the offer you accept through Setapp. Activation and license checks may require internet access. The CLI and automatic monitoring do not bypass these requirements.</p>
    <h3>Subscriptions, cancellation, and refunds</h3>
    <p>Review the price, trial conditions, renewal terms, and cancellation deadline shown by Setapp before subscribing. Manage subscription changes and cancellation through your Setapp account. Uninstalling DiskPress or Setapp does not cancel a subscription. For Setapp billing or refund requests, contact <a href="https://support.setapp.com/">Setapp support</a>, not Apple's App Store refund service. Applicable provider terms and consumer law determine eligibility.</p>
    <h3>Your files after access ends</h3>
    <p>If your Setapp access expires or is suspended, you may lose the ability to run further optimization or monitoring in this version. Files already optimized use native filesystem features and remain readable by macOS without DiskPress or an active subscription. There is no subscription-dependent format to unlock. Later edits or copies can still change the savings.</p>
    <p>Obtaining one version does not automatically license the other. A Mac App Store purchase and Setapp access are separate unless an offer explicitly states otherwise.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="privacy"><h2>Privacy and third-party services</h2><p>File optimization works offline in both versions. The Setapp version separately includes Setapp activation, licensing, and app-usage reporting. A failed application integrity check automatically opens a diagnostic webpage with a numeric check identifier. The website uses Plausible and hosting infrastructure. The <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> explains local app records, the differences between the two versions, website requests, and support messages.</p><p>Links to Apple, Setapp, developer websites, and other services are provided for convenience. Those services have their own terms and privacy practices. Your chosen AI agent or automation software also remains responsible for what it stores or transmits. DiskPress does not operate those third-party services.</p><p>DiskPress and this website are not sponsored or endorsed by Apple. Apple, Mac, macOS, and related marks belong to Apple Inc. Other product names and marks belong to their respective owners.</p></section>
  <section id="warranties"><h2>Warranties, liability, and consumer rights</h2><p>The applicable app license and distribution terms for your version govern any additional warranty and liability provisions. Subject to those terms and to the extent permitted by law, the app, website, and explanatory information are provided "as is" and "as available", without a promise of uninterrupted availability or suitability for every purpose.</p><p>Nothing in these terms excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded, overrides statutory guarantees, or reduces mandatory consumer protections, including any required refund or remedy. Any limitation applies only to the extent your applicable law permits. The website's explanatory content does not create a separate guarantee of storage savings or data recovery.</p></section>
  <section id="updates"><h2>Updates, availability, and contact</h2><p>The app and website may change as macOS, filesystem behavior, and product features evolve. There is no promise of support for every future operating-system version or third-party workflow. Downloads, updates, and availability also depend on Apple or Setapp for the version you use.</p><p>These terms may be revised for future use. The date above identifies the current version. This revision adds separate Mac App Store and Setapp licensing, billing, and privacy information. Revisions will not take away rights that applicable law protects.</p><p>For product help with either version, <a href="/support/">contact support</a> through GitHub or email. For questions about these terms, contact <a href={DEVELOPER_URL}>Ighor July</a> at <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.</p></section>
</DocumentLayout>
